  "summary": "This paper fabricated delaminated Ti3C2Tx films and five NH2-rGO:Ti3C2Tx heterostructure compositions (50:50, 20:80, 10:90, 5:95, and 1:99). Ti3C2Tx was produced by LiF/HCl etching and sonication delamination; composites were formed by shear mixing aminated rGO with d-Ti3C2Tx and vacuum filtration. The headline rGO : Ti3C2Tx (1 : 99) electrode achieved 256 F g\u22121 at 2 mV s\u22121 and retained 193 F g\u22121 at 100 mV s\u22121. Numeric capacitance values for pristine d-Ti3C2Tx and the 50:50, 20:80, and 10:90 composites were shown graphically but not printed; mass loading, BET area, pore properties, and volumetric/areal capacitances were not reported."
}